<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88051" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόμος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρό</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>foremost man,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόμαχος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.293
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.493
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀνήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.533
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινί</span>
			<i>opposed to</i> another <i>in the front rank,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				7.75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				116
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.85
			</span></i>: later, generally, <i>chief,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				200
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				410
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιῶν . . πρόμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					399
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γᾶς πρόμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					884
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατιῆς π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.233
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθηναίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν Πανελλήνων πρόμῳ
			Κίμωνι</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντων θεῶν θεὸς π.,</span> of
			the sun, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				660
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				361
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Phrygia</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰατρῶν π.</span> prob. ib.<i><span class="en">
				352
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Claudiopolis</span>). The forms <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόμνος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				904
			</span></i> (lyr.), and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πράμος</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				50
			</span></i>, are corrupt.</div>
